  "changelog": "0.3.4\n- New: Settings has a Devices section -- Speaker, Microphone and Camera -- that checks each one locally, without connecting to a Brain first. Set the speaker volume and play a test tone; set the microphone level and run a 3-second record-and-play-back check; open a webcam preview (it refreshes about once a second -- that's the check, not a fault; video inside a Brain session is full-speed).\n- The Settings panel moved from one crowded row of tabs to a left-hand list grouped into Network, Devices, Support and System.\n- The Camera preview needs a small extra component. Devices installed with 0.3.4 or later have it already; on an older device the Camera tab will say so, and Speaker and Microphone still work.",
